Suppose a secondary user continues to sense channel $m$ for $k$ mini-slots and obtains $k$ sensing results. The conditional probability that channel $m$ is available after the $k$th sensing mini-slot, denoted by $a_{m,k}$, can be derived as  egin{eqnarray} a_{m,k} & = & \Pr(S_m=0 \;|\; W_{m,1}=	heta_{m,1},\cdots,W_{m,k}=	heta_{m,k})
onumber \ & = &  rac{\Pr(W_{m,i}=	heta_{m,i},i=1,\cdots,k|S_m=0)\Pr(S_m=0)}{\sum_{j=0}^1 \Pr(W_{m,i}=	heta_{m,i},i=1,\cdots,k|S_m=j)\Pr(S_m=j)} 
onumber\ & = &  rac {\Pr(S_m=0)\prod_{i=1}^k\Pr(W_{m,i}=	heta_{m,i}|S_m=0)}{\sum_{j=0}^1 \Pr(S_m=j)\prod_{i=1}^k\Pr(W_{m,i}=	heta_{m,i}|S_m=j)} 
onumber \ & = & \left[ 1 +  rac{\Pr(S_m=1)}{\Pr(S_m=0)} \prod_{i=1}^k  rac{\Pr(W_{m,i}=	heta_{m,i}|S_m=1)}{\Pr(W_{m,i}=	heta_{m,i}|S_m=0)} ight]^{-1} 
onumber \ & = & \left[ 1 + \alpha_m^{d_m}  eta_m^{k-d_m}  rac{\Pr(S_m = 1)}{\Pr(S_m = 0)} ight]^{-1} 
onumber \ & = & \left( 1 + \alpha_m^{d_m}  eta_m^{k-d_m}  rac{\eta_m}{\zeta_m} ight)^{-1}_{,} \end{eqnarray} where $d_m$ is the number of observations whose sensing result is $0$ on channel $m$, and $\alpha_m$ and $ eta_m$ are defined as follows.

